@nsobid-97F9664CFB2721546954CDEB3B303A4C

# Super Mario RPG 1.0.1 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// Unity's NVN player creates the main window with 3 textures and picks how
// many are active from the device's max queued frames (clamped to 2..3),
// re-applying it with nvnWindowSetNumActiveTextures each frame. The device
// starts that value at 3 and the game never changes it, since the managed
// QualitySettings.maxQueuedFrames setter is stripped from this build.
// Starting it at 2, and building the window with 2 active textures, keeps
// the CPU at most one frame ahead of scanout.

@enabled
// GfxDevice max queued frames default
006B5EE8 48008052   // MOV W8,#2 (was MOV W8,#3)
// nvnWindowBuilderSetNumActiveTextures in NX_CreateBackBuffersAndWindow
006CB418 41008052   // MOV W1,#2 (was LDR W1,[X23], texture count 3)
@stop

// Reverse-engineered against Super Mario RPG 1.0.1 (Unity 2021.3.15f1, URP,
// IL2CPP). Names come from the game's own IL2CPP metadata; every offset was
// byte-verified against the IDB.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
